body:
Here are some examples:

``` js
// (a) Throws `no-extra-parens`
((function f() {})).length;

// (b) It doesn't throw anything
((function () {}))(1);

// (c) Throws `no-wrap-func` and `no-extra-parens`.
var x = (function g() {});
```

If `no-wrap-func` is supposed to be a particular case of `no-extra-parens`, shouldn't both rules throw for all the cases above?

If that is the case, it may make more sense to merge `no-wrap-func` into `no-extra-parens` as an option (`"all"`, `"functions-only"`).
